course: dictionary
lesson: 11044
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives weaver four meanings, so the words around it must tell you which one is meant. Ask yourself: what is the topic here? Birds, cloth, stories or a name?
explain: «Male weaver birds weave hanging nests from grass strips, tying knots with beak and feet.» Nests, grass and beaks are the clues, so a weaver here is a bird. The bird is the one doing the weaving, and the sentence is not about cloth at all.
explain: «For centuries most people learned jobs as apprentices, while guilds of bakers, weavers and builders set the rules.» Bakers and builders are people with jobs, so weavers must be people too, and the word means someone who makes cloth. Check by swapping in your meaning: "guilds of bakers, people who make cloth and builders" still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A weaver can be a person whose job or hobby is making cloth on a loom.
fact: A weaver, or weaverbird, is a small bird, mostly from Africa, that weaves nests from grass and leaves.
fact: A weaver of stories is someone who makes up and tells tales.
fact: Weaver is also a surname, the name of a family.
exercise: «Male weaver birds weave hanging nests from grass strips.» What is a weaver in this sentence? | A teller of stories | A person who makes cloth | *A small bird | A tangled piece of rope
exercise: «For centuries most people learned jobs as apprentices, while guilds of bakers, weavers and builders set the rules.» What does weavers mean here? | People who tell stories | *People who make cloth | Birds that build nests | Spiders that spin webs
exercise: «Birds are builders too: a weaver bird ties real knots in grass.» Find and copy the word that tells you weaver is an animal. | *bird | grass | knots | builders
test: «An orb-weaver spider waits on its sticky web and feels the vibrations of trapped insects.» What does weaver mean in orb-weaver? | A family name | A small bird from Africa | *A creature that spins webs | A person who makes cloth on a loom
test: In history, a «hand-loom weaver» worked at home on a loom until factories took over. What does weaver mean here? | A story-teller | *A person who makes cloth on a loom | A spider that spins webs | A bird that builds nests
exam: Jayden says weaver always means a bird. Is he right, and how do the clues in the sentences show it? | No, weaver only means a builder of houses | Yes, because only birds can weave | Yes, weaver always means a bird | *No, it can mean a cloth-maker, a bird, a storyteller or a surname, so the clues decide
